Title: Abraham and Isaac, Revisited
Credit: Written by
Author: David Joyner
Draft date: 2026-11-20
Notes: Draft 3 — animated short

[[ CHARACTER: name=abraham type=human gender=male build=narrow scale=0.48 label=Abraham ]]
[[ CHARACTER: name=isaac type=human gender=male build=broad scale=0.80 label=Isaac ]]

# 1. THE MANUSCRIPT

EXT. DESERT - OUTSIDE ABRAHAM'S CAVE - DAY

[[#1 | BEAT: Normal World / Opening Image | OBJ: Abraham perfects his account | SETUP: S01 manuscript]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=medium | SUBJECT=Abraham | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut | MARGIN=0.2 ]]

ABRAHAM (50s), a small, serious man with a scholar's posture, sits on a rock. He writes on a scroll headed GENESIS / B'RESHIT. [[beat: s01_takes_quill]] [[beat: s01_writes]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=insert | SUBJECT=scroll | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

INSERT - THE SCROLL: "AND ABRAHAM RAISED THE KNIFE." [[beat: s01_insert]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=medium | SUBJECT=Abraham | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut | MARGIN=0.2 ]]

Abraham studies the line and frowns. [[beat: s01_studies]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=insert | SUBJECT=scroll | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

INSERT - THE SCROLL: He turns the period into a question mark: "AND ABRAHAM RAISED THE KNIFE?" [[beat: s01_question_mark]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=medium | SUBJECT=Abraham | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut | MARGIN=0.2 ]]

From inside the cave: a tremendous THUD. He rolls up the scroll and tucks it into his belt. [[beat: s01_thud]]

# 2. THE INVINCIBLE

INT. ABRAHAM'S CAVE - DAY

[[#2 | BEAT: WTF / Reactions | OBJ: Abraham needs Isaac to cooperate | SETUP: S02 wrestling / S03 knife / S04 phone / S09 counting on fingers / S10 arms too short | PAYOFF: S02 initial]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

ISAAC (18), an enormous, cheerful wrestler, lifts a barbell made of two boulders and a log. He sets it down. THUD. He checks wrestling clips on his phone beside a stack of magazines. The top cover reads ISAAC THE INVINCIBLE. A coil of rope lies by the entrance. [[beat: s02_checks_clips]] [[beat: s02_rope_by_entrance]]

Abraham enters without knocking, a satchel over his shoulder and the scroll in his belt. [[beat: s02_abraham_enters]]

ISAAC
Dad! What about knocking? What if I was changing? [[beat: s02_knocking]]

ABRAHAM
I've been working on the Torah. Isaac, we must talk. [[beat: s02_must_talk]]

ISAAC
Can it wait? I have a match to study. [[beat: s02_match]]

ABRAHAM
I just spoke with God. [[beat: s02_spoke_with_god]]

ISAAC
Again with God? [[beat: s02_again]]

ABRAHAM
Watch that attitude. He says I have to sacrifice a son. [[beat: s02_attitude]]

Isaac finally looks up. [[beat: s02_looks_up]]

ISAAC
What about Ishmael? [[beat: s02_ishmael]]

ABRAHAM
Hagar said if I sacrifice Ishmael, I have to sleep outside. [[beat: s02_outside]]

ISAAC
Moooom! [[beat: s02_mom]]

ABRAHAM
Sarah's gathering rocks. [[beat: s02_rocks]]

Isaac holds up his magazine cover. [[beat: s02_magazine]]

ISAAC
Dad, I'm Isaac the Invincible. "Sacrificial lamb" doesn't fit my online persona. [[beat: s02_persona]]

ABRAHAM
I know. But it's the word of God. [[beat: s02_word_of_god]]

ISAAC
What were the exact words? [[beat: s02_exact_words]]

Abraham counts on his fingers. [[beat: s02_counts]]

ABRAHAM
Go to Mount Moriah. Build an altar. Tie you down. Raise my knife. Say a few words to teach Israel a lesson. And then... [[beat: s02_the_list]]

He has run out of fingers. He stares at his hand. [[beat: s02_out_of_fingers]]

ISAAC
And then?

ABRAHAM
That part escapes me. [[beat: s02_escapes_me]]

Isaac's phone BUZZES. He reads. [[beat: s02_buzz]]

ISAAC
My manager wants me to wrestle Friday. Can you drive me to Ocean City? [[beat: s02_ocean_city]]

ABRAHAM
Not if you're being sacrificed. Come on. [[beat: s02_come_on]]

Abraham grabs Isaac's wrist. Nothing moves. He braces both feet against the floor, pulls, slips, and lands on his back. [[beat: s02_pull]]

Isaac offers him a hand. Abraham accepts it and shoots upright like a cork. He clutches Isaac around the middle to steady himself. His arms do not reach halfway. [[beat: s02_cork_and_hug]]

ABRAHAM
Have you thought about a diet? [[beat: s02_diet]]

ISAAC
What are you sacrificing me with? [[beat: s02_sacrificing_with]]

Abraham draws a battered knife from his satchel. Isaac takes it by the handle. [[beat: s02_draws_knife]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=insert | SUBJECT=knife | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

The handle comes away in Isaac's fingers. [[beat: s02_knife_breaks]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=insert | SUBJECT=bowl | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

The blade drops into a wooden bowl with a CLANG. [[beat: s02_blade_in_bowl]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

ISAAC
That'll be a short ceremony. [[beat: s02_short_ceremony]]

ABRAHAM
God's going to be furious. [[beat: s02_furious]]

Isaac studies the blade, then the magazine, then his phone. [[beat: s02_handle_down]]

ISAAC
Wait. I got it. [[beat: s02_got_it]]

ABRAHAM
Got what?

Isaac tucks the barbell under one arm and strides out of the cave. Abraham drops the two pieces of the knife into his satchel, slings the coil of rope over his shoulder, and hurries after him. [[beat: s02_into_satchel]] [[beat: s02_slings_rope]] [[beat: s02_pockets_phone]]

# 3. THE CLIMB

EXT. PATH TO MOUNT MORIAH - DAY

[[#3 | BEAT: Connections / New Directions / Fun and Games | OBJ: Agree on a safe public ceremony | SETUP: S05 rope / S06 altar | PAYOFF: S02 physical contrast]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=pan-follow | TRANSITION=cut ]]

Isaac carries the log barbell on his shoulders. Abraham staggers after him with the coil of rope over his shoulder, the scroll in his belt, and a satchel holding the two pieces of the knife. [[beat: s03_climb]]

ISAAC
We go up the mountain. I build the altar. You tie me up. You raise what's left of that knife and tell everybody God doesn't want people sacrificing people. Then we substitute a lamb.

Abraham stops to catch his breath. Isaac stops with him, not breathing hard at all.

ABRAHAM
A morality lesson?

ISAAC
A challenge! "Sacrifice a Lamb for God." It'll be huge on TikTok.

ABRAHAM
We'll try it. But no improvising.

They walk on. Isaac bounds over a rock. Abraham climbs it on his hands and knees.

ISAAC
You sure you're up for this, Dad?

ABRAHAM
I am the father of nations.

He reaches the top. His sandal slips. Isaac catches him by the collar without putting down the barbell. Abraham dangles.

ISAAC
Where's the lamb?

ABRAHAM
I thought you brought the lamb.

ISAAC
I brought the altar.

ABRAHAM
God will provide.

ISAAC
He provided the knife.

Isaac sets his father on the path and walks on.

# 4. THE ALTAR

EXT. MOUNT MORIAH - DAY

[[#4 | BEAT: New Directions | OBJ: Rehearse the lesson harmlessly | PAYOFF: S06 altar / S04 phone | SETUP: S05 square knot / S07 livestream]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

Isaac drops the barbell. THUD. He pulls the two boulders off the log, sets them apart, and lays the log across them: a low altar. Abraham straightens a boulder; Isaac moves it back. They agree to leave it crooked. [[beat: s04_builds_altar]]

Isaac props his phone vertically against a smaller rock, its camera aimed at the altar. He strikes a heroic pose for the screen: fists on hips, chin up. Abraham tries the same pose. One fist finds a hip; the other hand ends up shading his eyes. [[beat: s04_props_phone]]

ISAAC
Remember: raise the handle, not the blade.

Abraham takes the two pieces of the knife out of his satchel, drops the blade back in, and keeps the wooden handle. Isaac sits on the altar and holds out his wrists. Abraham takes the coil from his shoulder and winds the rope around them. [[beat: s04_takes_pieces_out]] [[beat: s04_blade_into_satchel]] [[beat: s04_winds_rope]]

ISAAC
Looser. I'm supposed to escape after the speech.

ABRAHAM
I'm tying a bow.

ISAAC
That's a square knot. Give it here, I'll tie myself up.

ABRAHAM
I was tying knots before you were born.

He yanks the knot tight. Isaac tests it. It holds. He shrugs and lies back on the altar, propped on his elbows. [[beat: s04_yanks_knot]]

ISAAC
Press the red button when you're ready. Then I'll say my part.

Abraham picks up the phone. [[beat: s04_picks_up_phone]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=insert | SUBJECT=phone | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

ON THE SCREEN: a big red LIVE button. [[beat: s04_red_button]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

Abraham nods. He rehearses silently, counting on his fingers, hands shaking. He goes to lean the phone back against its rock.

# 5. LIVE

EXT. MOUNT MORIAH - CONTINUOUS

[[#5 | BEAT: Disconnections / All Is Lost | OBJ: Abraham wants to control the ceremony | PAYOFF: S03 knife / S07 livestream / S09 counting on fingers | TURN: The staged ritual becomes an actual choice]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=insert | SUBJECT=phone | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

The phone slips in Abraham's shaking hands. He catches it. His thumb lands on the red button. [[beat: s05_goes_live]]

ON THE SCREEN: LIVE. The viewer count climbs. [[beat: s05_count_climbs]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

Abraham props the phone on its rock and backs away from it. [[beat: s05_props_phone]]

ISAAC
Dad. We're on. [[beat: s05_were_on]]

ABRAHAM
I wasn't ready.

ISAAC
Nobody's ever ready. Go.

Abraham faces the phone. He raises the wooden handle in one hand and counts on the fingers of the other.

ABRAHAM
People of Israel. God said to me: go to Mount Moriah. Build an altar. Tie down my son. Raise my knife --

The satchel slips from his shoulder. The blade slides out, CLATTERS across the altar, and sticks point-first in the log, inches from Isaac's arm. [[beat: s05_blade]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=medium | SUBJECT=Isaac | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=hold ]]

For once, Isaac has no comeback.

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=insert | SUBJECT=phone | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

ON THE SCREEN: the viewer count doubles. A comment scrolls past: "IS THAT A REAL KNIFE" [[beat: s05_count_doubles]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=medium | SUBJECT=Abraham | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=hold ]]

ABRAHAM
And then...

He has run out of fingers. He looks at the blade. At Isaac. At the watching phone.

ISAAC
(quietly)
And then?

# 6. THE REVISION

EXT. MOUNT MORIAH - CONTINUOUS

[[#6 | BEAT: Race to the Finish / Finale / Final Image | OBJ: Abraham chooses his son | PAYOFF: S01 manuscript / S03 knife / S05 rope / S07 livestream / S10 arms too short / S08 relatives]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

Abraham sets the handle on the ground, far from the blade. He turns his back on the phone and faces his son. [[beat: s06_handle_down]]

ABRAHAM
I can't remember what God said next. So I'll say it. And then I take my son home.

He pulls at Isaac's knot. It will not budge. He tries with his teeth.

ISAAC
Told you. Square knot.

ABRAHAM
(through the rope)
Not now.

ISAAC
Dad, you're still live.

ABRAHAM
Then let them hear it. God doesn't want us sacrificing one another.

Abraham puts his arms around Isaac's shoulders, as far as they will go. Isaac flexes -- the rope snaps, and its two halves fly off his wrists and land in the dirt on either side of the altar. His arms close all the way around his father. They tumble backward off the low altar, still hugging. [[beat: s06_rope_snaps]]

Isaac recovers the phone. The viewer count climbs again. [[beat: s06_recovers_phone]] [[beat: s06_count_climbs_again]]

ISAAC
That was awesome. I'm calling it the "Don't Sacrifice Your Son" challenge.

ABRAHAM
I preferred the lamb.

ISAAC
So... Ocean City Friday?

Abraham looks at the broken knife, then at Isaac.

ABRAHAM
I'll drive.

He takes the scroll from his belt and unrolls it, pulls a quill from the satchel, and crosses out THE KNIFE and its question mark. He writes two words and a period in their place. [[beat: s06_scroll_from_belt]] [[beat: s06_unrolls]] [[beat: s06_takes_quill]] [[beat: s06_revision]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=insert | SUBJECT=scroll | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=hold ]]

INSERT - THE SCROLL: "AND ABRAHAM RAISED HIS SON." [[beat: s06_insert]]

[[ CAMERA: FRAMING=wide | SUBJECT=ensemble | MOVE=static | TRANSITION=cut ]]

Isaac's phone BUZZES.

ISAAC
Uncle Nahor and Aunt Milcah commented. "Saw the stream. We're at your cave. Where is everybody?"

ABRAHAM
They're at the cave?

ISAAC
With luggage.

Abraham bolts up the mountain, away from home, the open scroll in his hand. Isaac catches him in three easy strides, hoists him overhead like a championship belt, and keeps running. [[beat: s06_quill_away]] [[beat: s06_bolts]]

The scroll trails behind them like a banner.

FADE OUT.
